The evidence packet is written: `docs/content-analysis/perspective-reviews/Madonna/2026-10-12_212806/evidence-packet.md`. The subject and SHA match `context.json`, and the frozen draft and live draft were not touched.

**Largest unresolved evidence gap:** the childhood mechanism the thesis rests on has one witness, Madonna herself, and her own accounts conflict.

- **The "take control" quote is in the wrong moment.** In Time's 1985 "Madonna on Madonna" sidebar she places that decision on the couch with her sick mother, before the hospitalization and death. The draft places it after the death, inside the grieving household.
- **"The House That Never Cried" is contradicted by her 1985 account.** The same Time piece has her saying "It is awful to see your father cry." The 2015 Stern passage the draft quotes also includes "I think he was devastated too," which the blockquote drops.
- **No independent account of the household exists in the packet.** The only sibling on record, Christopher, disputed her handling of the story, not the facts. Statements by her father or other siblings were not searched.

Other discrepancies the packet records for the evaluators:

- **Thesis blockquote wording.** Vanity Fair's archive prints "I still have to prove that I'm Somebody"; the draft has "prove that Somebody."
- **American Life quote.** Her statement reads "I do not believe it is appropriate to air it at this time"; the draft's quoted words match a newspaper paraphrase. The statement came about three weeks before the album, and "worst seller of her career" is supported only as of 2005.
- **Type 8 tiebreaker.** The 2023 Instagram post the draft uses as image-defense also says "I have never apologised… and I'm not going to start… Bow down, bitches!"
- **2026 VMA speech.** She corrected "my manager" to "the assistant to the manager" mid-anecdote, and in 2012 said of the same night "I didn't feel that I had lost anything."
- **bell hooks.** The vogueing point attributed to her does not appear in the partial text I could read; the book itself was not consulted.

Still unverified: no film or video was viewed (including *Truth or Dare*), four Jay Shetty lines exist only in auto-captions, and every July–October 2026 event rests on press pages fetched this week.

The packet has 53 claims (CLM-01 to CLM-12 are the load-bearing ones), 17 listed disputes, and a 53-row source ledger.

I also added one note to memory: the second-pass quote checker skipped quotes carried over from the older draft, which is how the Vanity Fair wording went unchecked since July.
